{"shortDescription":"Asia's diesel markets continued to see December refiner spot offers, with deals done in larger discounts month on month so far, though the backwardation structure in paper markets firmed and cash differential rebounded.More offers surfaced from northeast Asian refiners for December shipments, with…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia's diesel markets continued to see December refiner spot offers, with deals done in larger discounts month on month so far, though the backwardation structure in paper markets firmed and cash differential rebounded."]},{"type":"p","children":["More offers surfaced from northeast Asian refiners for December shipments, with at least one more South Korea seller in the market."]},{"type":"p","children":["A slew of deals in the early week have all been done at discounts of $2-3 a barrel, though some cargoes were also sold at discounts of slightly larger than $3 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["So far, limited shipping enquiries were in the market for diesel shipments west."]},{"type":"p","children":["Refining margins (GO10SGCKMc1) were little changed from the previous session at around $53.50 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["Cash differentials (GO10-SIN-DIF) gained slightly, tracking the steeper backwardation in paper markets - though window spot activity remained absent."]},{"type":"p","children":["The jet fuel arbitrage window between Asia and the West remained profitable, against a backdrop of falling freight costs, according to trade sources."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some deals for December loading jet fuel were done at small premiums still as a result, with more offers emerging from two refiners and discussions underway."]},{"type":"p","children":["Regrade (JETREG10SGMc1) narrowed slightly to discounts of 10 cent a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["SINGAPORE CASH DEALS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- No deal for gasoil or jet fuel"]},{"type":"p","children":["INVENTO